1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
<font color="#20e020">HI removed, cleaned
and corrected by Lunar Team</font>

2
00:00:31,614 --> 00:00:33,407
Excuse me.

3
00:00:34,325 --> 00:00:36,452
What kind of tree is this?

4
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:38,245
Couldn't say.

5
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:42,458
Smells good. So you're not a local?

6
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:47,296
Born five miles down the road.
Just don't give a crap about trees.

7
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:03,812
Name's Justin Prentiss.

8
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:07,149
Student at a private-school operation
a couple miles from here.

9
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:09,818
They realized he was missing
around 6 this morning...

10
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:12,946
...activated the electronic monitoring
device on his ankle...

11
00:01:13,114 --> 00:01:15,991
- ...found him and called us at 8.
- Estimated time of death?

12
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:19,787
Coroner puts time of death somewhere
between 10 and 1 last night.

13
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:22,831
I wanted to take him down
soon as Forensics were done.

14
00:01:22,999 --> 00:01:25,125
But per your request,
we didn't touch him.

15
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:27,878
We won't be long.
You can have him soon as we're done.

16
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:30,881
- What's with the ankle bracelet?
- Good question.

17
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:33,342
Mr. Maclean.

18
00:01:37,305 --> 00:01:40,057
This is the principal of the school,
Asher Maclean.

19
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:42,559
These people are from the CBI.
They wanna know...

20
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:46,522
...why your student has an electronic
monitoring device on him.

21
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:48,690
Justin had some truancy issues
recently.

22
00:01:48,858 --> 00:01:51,401
- Hence the device.
- What kind of school is this?

23
00:01:51,569 --> 00:01:54,196
Bright Arch is a wilderness program
for troubled youth.

24
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:57,407
- Like a summer camp?
- No, we're an accredited high school.

25
00:01:57,575 --> 00:02:00,202
Students stay at Bright Arch
for a year on average.

26
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:03,705
We provide structure and discipline
through interaction with nature.

27
00:02:03,873 --> 00:02:07,501
Plus the regular high-school curriculum,
of course.

28
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:10,337
Hm.

29
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:14,216
She doesn't like you,
and you don't like her.

30
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:18,053
- Why is that?
- No comment.

31
00:02:19,222 --> 00:02:21,014
Chief Brody?

32
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:23,100
Why don't you like him?

33
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:26,562
- What has that got to do with anything?
- I'm just curious.

34
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:28,772
Think you might show
a little more respect.

35
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:31,358
- Respect for...?
- There is a dead child here.

36
00:02:31,526 --> 00:02:35,404
Yes. Yes, he's dead.
He doesn't care how I talk to you.

37
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:42,578
I've never worked with the CBI.
All your units come with a clown?

38
00:02:42,745 --> 00:02:46,456
- We get the job done.
- Well, how about getting it done now...

39
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:50,210
...so we can take this kid out of here?
How would that be?

40
00:02:51,254 --> 00:02:52,754
Yeah. We'll do that.

41
00:02:52,922 --> 00:02:55,591
Yep, you can take him.
I got the basic facts.

42
00:02:55,758 --> 00:02:58,260
- Oh, is that right? That quick, huh?
- Yeah.

43
00:02:58,428 --> 00:02:59,803
You wanna enlighten us?

44
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:03,765
Oh, Forensics probably told you
a lot of it already, I would guess.

45
00:03:03,933 --> 00:03:05,726
His knuckles and his knees suggest...

46
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:08,770
...that he was overpowered
in a hand-to-hand struggle.

47
00:03:08,938 --> 00:03:12,107
The blow to the head
was the coup de grâce.

48
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:16,778
But the ground around him
is relatively undisturbed...

49
00:03:16,946 --> 00:03:20,115
...which means that the struggle
would have taken place elsewhere.

50
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:22,951
Uphill, presumably.

51
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:26,455
Injured animals tend
to move downhill, of course.

52
00:03:26,623 --> 00:03:28,582
Do you have any actual facts?

53
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:31,585
It's an actual fact
that you dislike Mr. Maclean here...

54
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:34,463
...because he's a tree-hugging,
liberal wacko...

55
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:36,673
...who's probably running
some kind of cult.

56
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:40,093
He dislikes you because you're
a small-minded provincial hayseed.

57
00:03:40,261 --> 00:03:43,305
Not that you are, necessarily.
That's just what he thinks.

58
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:45,682
Facts pertaining to this poor boy.

59
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:51,813
There was no moon last night,
so it was very dark.

60
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:55,651
Justin wouldn't have been able
to move very far, injured as he was.

61
00:03:55,818 --> 00:03:58,487
He had a lot of dirt in his hair...

62
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:01,949
...lot of dirt in his ears,
and deep up under his nails.

63
00:04:02,116 --> 00:04:07,663
So somewhere close by,
somewhere very close by...

64
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:10,624
...there's a spot where someone...

65
00:04:13,169 --> 00:04:15,337
Where someone buried him alive.

66
00:04:15,505 --> 00:04:18,006
Oh, my God.

67
00:04:32,021 --> 00:04:34,690
All right, all right, all right.

68
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:38,694
Settle down, folks. Take your seats.

69
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:40,362
Over here, I got you a spot.

70
00:04:40,863 --> 00:04:42,906
Let's go.

71
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:47,202
- I heard he got buried alive.
- Cut it out, man.

72
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:50,247
I know the last couple of days
have been rough.

73
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:52,207
Losing Justin hurts...

74
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:58,130
...but his death cannot become
your crutch for a negative attitude.

75
00:04:58,923 --> 00:05:03,176
You can learn and grow
from this experience.

76
00:05:05,138 --> 00:05:06,263
Bryan.

77
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:10,267
Sir, do we still get to do the sacred
fire ceremony on Friday?

78
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:14,354
I think there's all the more reason
to do it now. We need healing.

79
00:05:14,939 --> 00:05:16,356
All right, listen, kids.

80
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:19,359
The strangers you see here
are detectives...

81
00:05:19,527 --> 00:05:23,739
...that will be investigating
the situation with Justin.

82
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:26,616
They are here to find out
what happened to him...

83
00:05:26,784 --> 00:05:32,581
...and I want all of you to answer
any questions they have as best you can.

84
00:05:33,041 --> 00:05:36,668
- Yes, yes, yes, people?
- Yes, yes, yes!

85
00:05:37,795 --> 00:05:40,088
Is it true that he was buried alive?

86
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:42,257
- Orrin...
- Oh, yeah, that is true.

87
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:43,467
- What?
- That's true?

88
00:05:43,676 --> 00:05:45,427
- Who did it?
- That's enough, Elliot.

89
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:50,932
Let's all get back to our classes quickly.
We're wasting daylight.

90
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:54,895
You guys talk to the counselors. We'll
press the principal, see what he knows.

91
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:56,438
We'll talk to the kids last.

92
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:59,441
- Mr. Maclean, I wanted to...
- Agent Lisbon, excuse me.

93
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:00,984
Orrin.

94
00:06:01,194 --> 00:06:06,448
We speak only when recognized
as part of the discussion.

95
00:06:07,116 --> 00:06:09,201
Okay? Get out of here.

96
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:10,994
I'm sorry about that.

97
00:06:11,204 --> 00:06:14,956
Well, welcome to Bright Arch.
Shall we convene in my office?

98
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:16,416
Yes, yes, yes.

99
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:19,252
Honey, try to calm down, okay?
We'll find everything...

100
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:20,921
- You son of a bitch.
- Calm down.

101
00:06:21,089 --> 00:06:23,256
What happened? What happened?
What did you do?

102
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:28,428
- Mr. Prentiss, David, let's be calm now.
- Step back, sir. Now.

103
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:31,807
It's okay. It's okay.

104
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:35,143
This man was supposed
to look after my son.

105
00:06:35,311 --> 00:06:38,480
It's his responsibility
to keep his students safe, and he didn't.

106
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:42,109
- He didn't.
- David.

107
00:06:42,276 --> 00:06:45,028
Mr. Prentiss, let's go and talk.
This way.

108
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:47,322
This way, now.

109
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:54,454
How did you learn about Bright Arch?

110
00:06:54,997 --> 00:06:59,835
One of David's colleagues has a child
who had gone way off track...

111
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:02,963
...and they saw very positive results
from the program.

112
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:07,175
- Justin was misbehaving?
- He changed a lot over the last year.

113
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:11,555
Suddenly, he was always locked
in his room, dour, uncommunicative.

114
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:13,348
Violent on occasion.

115
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:17,144
- Therapy didn't work.
- What kind of violence did he engage in?

116
00:07:17,311 --> 00:07:20,647
He often shouted at me
and would threaten his father.

117
00:07:20,815 --> 00:07:24,526
Just shouting? No physical abuse?
No criminal behavior?

118
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:26,194
No.

119
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:34,494
Please find out who did this.

120
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,330
Please.

121
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:43,378
Kids love the drama of things like this.
I hope it can be resolved quickly.

122
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:48,717
You know, you look like Burt Reynolds
in this shot.

123
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:56,224
- How long has Bright Arch been running?
- Almost 10 years now.

124
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:58,101
- That was all of the students?
- Yes.

125
00:07:58,311 --> 00:08:00,604
We like to keep
a low counselor-student ratio...

126
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:04,441
...so that everyone gets the focused
individual attention that they need.

127
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:06,526
Right. What's the pitch?

128
00:08:07,904 --> 00:08:10,363
- I don't follow.
- The pitch, the gimmick, the hook.

129
00:08:10,531 --> 00:08:12,908
How do you sell this place
to prospective parents?

130
00:08:13,075 --> 00:08:15,744
We don't have to sell it.
They come by word of mouth.

131
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:19,206
This is a simple, natural,
healing community...

132
00:08:19,373 --> 00:08:22,709
...where your troubled and
underachieving sons and daughters...

133
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:25,754
...are encouraged to get in touch
with their inner resources.

134
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:27,130
Encouraged how?

135
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,925
By a code of honor and discipline.

136
00:08:30,092 --> 00:08:32,761
By learning wilderness skills
and teamwork...

137
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:35,722
...through an up-close experience
with Mother Nature.

138
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:38,433
- That's a good pitch.
- It's a good program.

139
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:44,814
- Yes, Cassie?
- I got your tea.

140
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:46,900
Oh, thank you.

141
00:08:57,370 --> 00:09:00,288
One of our great success stories.

142
00:09:00,456 --> 00:09:03,833
Arrived here about nine months ago
angry and withdrawn.

143
00:09:04,001 --> 00:09:06,503
- She's blossomed wonderfully.
- Tell me about Justin.

144
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:09,130
Why was he wearing an
electronic monitoring device?

145
00:09:09,298 --> 00:09:11,132
I didn't see anyone else wearing one.

146
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:13,301
Justin had only been with us
three months.

147
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:15,303
He was still in the rebellious phase.

148
00:09:15,471 --> 00:09:19,307
The day before yesterday, he left
without permission for several hours.

149
00:09:19,475 --> 00:09:22,018
He refused to tell us where he had been
and with whom.

150
00:09:22,186 --> 00:09:25,772
His punishment was eight hours
in the reflection room...

151
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:29,818
...and the electronic monitoring device
for two weeks.

152
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:31,319
Confinement and dog collars.

153
00:09:31,487 --> 00:09:36,658
Yeah, that'll certainly encourage
the discovery of inner resources, I guess.

154
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:38,952
Do the parents know
that's part of the deal?

155
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:42,831
It's in the brochure. Page 3.

156
00:09:44,542 --> 00:09:46,418
So you must get a lot of problem kids.

157
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:52,215
How do you handle the psychos that
won't knuckle under, no matter what?

158
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:54,217
We don't take them in the first place.

159
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:57,637
- I vet thoroughly every acceptance.
- No name jumped in your head...

160
00:09:57,805 --> 00:09:59,973
- ...when you heard about the murder?
- No.

161
00:10:01,225 --> 00:10:04,352
- You ever heard of Z Krew?
- No. What's that?

162
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:09,691
- I'd like to talk to Justin's friends.
- Of course.

163
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:12,861
- He was in Missy Jenkins' teaching pod.
- Great.

164
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:17,240
Bear in mind that I, or one of my
staff members, need to be present...

165
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:20,493
- ...before you talk with our students.
- Is that right?

166
00:10:20,661 --> 00:10:23,038
- It's the law.
- Really?

167
00:10:30,004 --> 00:10:31,212
I hate the woods.

168
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:34,841
Would you rather be playing desk jockey
with Van Pelt right now?

169
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:40,221
Who sends their kids to a place like this?
It's not cheap either.

170
00:10:40,389 --> 00:10:42,390
A little discipline is good for the soul.

171
00:10:42,558 --> 00:10:45,393
Yeah, but this is like
a juvie prison camp.

172
00:10:45,561 --> 00:10:49,397
No. This is like spring break in Cancun
compared to juvie.

173
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:52,400
Wait, you were in juvenile hall?
Seriously?

174
00:10:52,568 --> 00:10:55,070
- Yeah. Didn't you read my file?
- No.

175
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:58,073
- Wait, did you read mine?
- Of course.

176
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:00,700
What do you got?

177
00:11:09,043 --> 00:11:11,086
Interesting, huh?

178
00:11:12,213 --> 00:11:14,214
Maybe there's treasure involved.

179
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:18,134
- Maybe not.
- Follow the trail. Find out.

180
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:25,725
Now over and under...

181
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:30,647
...over and under and through.

182
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:32,816
Simple. Again.

183
00:11:33,025 --> 00:11:37,612
Over and under and over...

184
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,781
- Hey, come on.
- ...and under.

185
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:43,785
Chris, hit the reflection room.

186
00:11:46,455 --> 00:11:47,747
One hour.

187
00:11:47,915 --> 00:11:49,791
Marley, give me 25.

188
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:52,669
- But he started it.
- Yeah, I hear you and I do not care.

189
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:54,462
Twenty-five.

190
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:56,339
Hey, lady.

191
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:59,634
- Are you talking to me?
- Yeah, I'm talking to you.

192
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,553
This is important. Look at me.

193
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:04,472
CBI. That's police,
there'll no backchat.

194
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:07,767
- You do exactly as I tell you.
- What?

195
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:09,561
Hold this.

196
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:16,484
CBI. California Bureau of Investigation.

197
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:19,612
Well, ma'am,
we have reason to believe...

198
00:12:27,955 --> 00:12:31,166
- Untie me this instant.
- Sorry, ma'am.

199
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:34,043
- Mr. Maclean, told me to do that.
- No, he didn't.

200
00:12:34,211 --> 00:12:37,088
Yes, he did. He's in his office right now.
Go and ask him.

201
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:48,808
My people, we have precious little time
until our friend returns.

202
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:52,020
I need to know who knows most
about what around here.

203
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:55,648
Elliot's been here like two years,
so he knows everything.

204
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:58,193
That's a long time
to be stuck out in the woods.

205
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:01,154
- I like it here.
- So, what's the deal with Justin?

206
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:04,866
- Who disliked him?
- Nobody. He was fine.

207
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:08,661
- You say that like he was a prize jerk.
- No, he wouldn't win any prizes.

208
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:15,376
I mean, he was basically a good kid,
but he just fought a lot. With everybody.

209
00:13:15,544 --> 00:13:18,379
What do you think he was doing
out in the woods?

210
00:13:20,549 --> 00:13:23,593
- Who knows?
- The woods are a bad place.

211
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:27,347
- Yeah? Why's that?
- The axman Zachariah lives there.

212
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:29,140
Shh.

213
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:33,728
- Who's Zachariah?
- There is no Zachariah.

214
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:35,522
It's just a story.

215
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:38,233
- Yeah, I was just kidding.
- No, you weren't.

216
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:42,737
Come on, guys. Aren't you a little old
to believe in stuff like that?

217
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:44,906
A year ago...

218
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:47,951
...they found a townie kid
dead in the woods.

219
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:49,786
He'd been chopped up with a ax.

220
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:53,665
His head was 20 feet up in a tree,
with a crazy look on his face.

221
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:58,878
Okay. Now, does Zachariah
have anything to do with Z Krew?

222
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:08,096
- Was Justin in Z Krew?
- Jane?

223
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:09,764
Jane.

224
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:12,767
What the hell are you playing at?
You can't tie people up.

225
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:15,395
- Yeah, sorry.
- I should think you would be.

226
00:14:16,188 --> 00:14:18,273
My apologies, Mr. Maclean.

227
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:21,442
We'll be back tomorrow morning
if that's convenient.

228
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:23,778
See you in the morning.

229
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:27,615
I hope you got something useful
for the trouble you caused.

230
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:30,493
Yes, I did. The story
of the mad axman Zachariah...

231
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:32,287
...who lives in these here woods.

232
00:14:32,454 --> 00:14:33,663
- Z.
- Yes, Z.

233
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:36,583
I would have gotten more,
but you came back too quickly.

234
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:40,837
Reality check. I'm your
supervising agent. I'm not your decoy.

235
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:48,761
So, what'd it say?

236
00:14:48,929 --> 00:14:51,973
- What?
- You know, my file.

237
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:55,351
- You haven't read your own file?
- No. It's against the rules.

238
00:14:55,519 --> 00:14:56,811
You're kidding.

239
00:14:56,979 --> 00:15:00,189
What? I like rules.
Why be a cop if you don't like rules?

240
00:15:00,357 --> 00:15:01,649
Come on. What'd it say?

241
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:05,153
You know what it says. It's your life.
I didn't know you were adopted.

242
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:08,239
- But other than that, no surprises.
- Adopted? What?

243
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:10,116
Kidding.

244
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:12,160
Ha-ha. Very funny.

245
00:15:13,495 --> 00:15:17,457
- So why were you in juvie?
- You know, the usual reasons.

246
00:15:27,843 --> 00:15:30,720
That house is marked on this map
with a skull and crossbones.

247
00:15:30,888 --> 00:15:33,139
What are the usual reasons
for being in juvie?

248
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:35,516
I'll tell you all about it sometime.

249
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:40,396
Hey, check this out.

250
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:49,072
- Looks like Justin's shoe.
- Yep.

251
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:52,367
- I'll call Forensics, mark it up.
- Yeah.

252
00:15:59,541 --> 00:16:02,377
- Hello?
- CBI.

253
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:05,213
Anybody home?

254
00:16:05,714 --> 00:16:07,590
Hello?

255
00:16:14,932 --> 00:16:16,516
CBI.

256
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:21,312
- Try the other side?
- Yeah.

257
00:16:26,402 --> 00:16:30,947
You move, you die,
you Mameluke sons of bitches.

258
00:16:35,035 --> 00:16:36,911
- Kneel down.
- Hey, we're cops.

259
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:39,163
Kneel!

260
00:16:40,165 --> 00:16:43,459
I'm gonna blow your damn faces off you,
you hear?

261
00:16:43,669 --> 00:16:45,128
- Hey, hey, Winston.
- I'm gonna...

262
00:16:45,295 --> 00:16:48,923
Winston, you fool,
put that gun down. Let go.

263
00:16:49,383 --> 00:16:51,259
God.

264
00:16:53,929 --> 00:16:55,722
- Thank you.
- No problem.

265
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:58,099
Yeah, thanks.
What are you doing here?

266
00:16:58,559 --> 00:17:01,561
Winston called 911.
Lucky, I was close.

267
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:05,273
Can you please tell me
why I'm still here?

268
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:08,151
I had nothing to do
with that kid who died. Nothing.

269
00:17:08,318 --> 00:17:11,446
You assaulted us. If you wanna talk
about Justin, that's fine.

270
00:17:11,613 --> 00:17:13,448
How am I supposed to know
who you are?

271
00:17:13,615 --> 00:17:18,786
You're banging on my doors, "CBI, CBI."
That's supposed to mean something?

272
00:17:18,954 --> 00:17:20,830
Yeah, we do need
better brand awareness.

273
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:24,250
But your response was disproportionate.
Your brandished a firearm.

274
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:25,460
So here we are.

275
00:17:26,795 --> 00:17:31,466
My security alarm went off.
I was loaded. I reacted.

276
00:17:31,633 --> 00:17:33,801
- That's all.
- You're very security conscious.

277
00:17:33,969 --> 00:17:35,136
- Why is that?
- Why not?

278
00:17:35,804 --> 00:17:39,640
- Are there people who dislike security?
- What's been your history of contact...

279
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:45,772
- ...with the students from Bright Arch?
- Zero. I have a zero history of contact.

280
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:55,490
You know the kid who was killed,
Justin Prentiss...

281
00:17:55,657 --> 00:17:58,284
...who was buried
close to your property line?

282
00:17:58,452 --> 00:18:01,829
He had a map that showed your house
marked with a skull and crossbones.

283
00:18:01,997 --> 00:18:04,540
- I don't know what that means.
- How about Zachariah?

284
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:06,834
- That name ring any bells?
- No.

285
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:13,883
- Looks like it's gonna be a long night.
- I just wanna be left alone.

286
00:18:14,051 --> 00:18:16,511
And I want those kids
to leave me alone.

287
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:19,347
They go up to my property,
mess with my stuff.

288
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:22,517
They break windows,
they spray paint my doors...

289
00:18:22,684 --> 00:18:27,563
...pull all kinds of stunts all night,
like a routine.

290
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:29,649
Okay. So, what did you do
in response?

291
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:33,528
I did everything to try and stop them,
short of actual violence.

292
00:18:33,695 --> 00:18:39,700
I built fences. I planted poison oak.
I installed alarms.

293
00:18:39,868 --> 00:18:42,370
They just took it all like it was a game.

294
00:18:42,538 --> 00:18:45,248
- Were they at your house last night?
- The night before.

295
00:18:45,415 --> 00:18:49,210
Three or four of them,
throwing balloons of red paint.

296
00:18:50,587 --> 00:18:53,589
Would you be able to identify
any of the kids if you saw them?

297
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:55,716
They always wore masks.

298
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:14,944
I wanna apologize
for the misunderstanding yesterday.

299
00:19:15,112 --> 00:19:17,363
Mr. Jane will comport himself
properly today.

300
00:19:17,531 --> 00:19:18,573
Yes, I will.

301
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:23,369
Who's Zachariah?

302
00:19:24,955 --> 00:19:26,455
- Who?
- Zachariah.

303
00:19:26,623 --> 00:19:28,541
- Never heard of him. Who is he?
- Liar.

304
00:19:28,834 --> 00:19:30,543
- Liar?
- Pants on fire.

305
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:34,255
- They're ablaze.
- I wanna cooperate with you people.

306
00:19:34,423 --> 00:19:37,925
But this man is... I don't know
what he is trying to do, but I resent it.

307
00:19:38,093 --> 00:19:40,094
You sound more than a little paranoid...

308
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:43,264
This is what I'm talking about.
How is this police work?

309
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:45,766
Oh, I'm kidding with you. I get bored.

310
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:47,935
The thing is,
you have heard of Zachariah.

311
00:19:48,103 --> 00:19:51,105
You know who Zachariah is,
and you're scared of Zachariah.

312
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:55,443
- And we're gonna find out why.
- Let's put a pin in that, shall we?

313
00:19:56,111 --> 00:19:59,155
We have information putting Justin
at Mr. Winston's house...

314
00:19:59,364 --> 00:20:00,615
...the night he went AWOL.

315
00:20:00,782 --> 00:20:05,077
He went there on a regular basis with
a group of kids to torment Mr. Winston.

316
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:08,831
- So says Mr. Winston. Has he any proof?
- Why would he lie?

317
00:20:08,999 --> 00:20:12,793
Because he's a crazy old man
with a grudge against this school.

318
00:20:12,961 --> 00:20:15,171
Perhaps he's crazy enough
to do something.

319
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:18,466
He's complained plenty of times.
There's never reality to it.

320
00:20:18,634 --> 00:20:20,426
Chief Brody disagrees.

321
00:20:20,594 --> 00:20:24,096
She thinks some of your students
are vandals and you're protecting them.

322
00:20:24,264 --> 00:20:28,100
Chief Brody is a small-town cop.
She gets ideas in her head.

323
00:20:28,268 --> 00:20:31,270
Look, the truth is that nobody
around here likes us very much.

324
00:20:31,438 --> 00:20:35,191
They think the kids are all drug addicts
and delinquents. They're scared.

325
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:37,693
You mind if we sit down
with some students...

326
00:20:37,903 --> 00:20:40,154
...to ask them
about Mr. Winston's allegations?

327
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:42,990
Not at all.

328
00:20:43,158 --> 00:20:47,662
As long as you follow
proper legal protocol.

329
00:20:50,165 --> 00:20:51,207
Of course.

330
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:54,418
Hey, hey, hey.

331
00:20:54,795 --> 00:20:58,839
Agent Lisbon of the CBI
would like to talk to you for a moment.

332
00:20:59,007 --> 00:21:03,010
Let's all listen with respectful attention,
all right?

333
00:21:03,178 --> 00:21:05,179
Yes, sir.

334
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:09,850
Jane, they're all yours.

335
00:21:13,647 --> 00:21:16,440
- Hello, kids.
- Hello.

336
00:21:16,858 --> 00:21:18,401
That's the best you got?

337
00:21:18,568 --> 00:21:19,652
Hello, kids.

338
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:23,698
- Hello.
- Thank you. Thank you.

339
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:27,910
Who wants to see some magic?

340
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:29,745
- Hands?
- I do.

341
00:21:29,955 --> 00:21:31,247
Good.

342
00:21:33,208 --> 00:21:34,583
Watch me closely.

343
00:21:39,589 --> 00:21:40,673
Concentrate.

344
00:21:44,594 --> 00:21:46,721
Make sure I don't do anything sneaky.

345
00:21:46,888 --> 00:21:49,223
- All right, this is ridiculous.
- Hush.

346
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:51,767
Watching my hands.

347
00:21:59,234 --> 00:22:00,693
I'm gonna need a volunteer.

348
00:22:02,904 --> 00:22:04,697
You.

349
00:22:06,366 --> 00:22:08,617
Stand up. Come here.

350
00:22:13,915 --> 00:22:16,250
- Name?
- Orrin.

351
00:22:16,418 --> 00:22:18,127
Well, Orrin, today's your lucky day.

352
00:22:18,295 --> 00:22:21,756
I'm gonna look into your mind
and I am gonna read your thoughts.

353
00:22:33,602 --> 00:22:36,979
You're thinking, "Gosh,
I hope he can't read my thoughts...

354
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:40,649
...because then he'd know
that I was up in the woods with Justin...

355
00:22:40,817 --> 00:22:42,318
...the night before he died...

356
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:45,279
...throwing paint bombs
at the old crazy man's door."

357
00:22:51,745 --> 00:22:53,162
Orrin, that was kind of dumb.

358
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:56,248
You should have thought
of something a little more innocent.

359
00:22:59,836 --> 00:23:02,421
We're gonna have to have a little talk.

360
00:23:04,674 --> 00:23:06,175
Follow me.

361
00:23:06,343 --> 00:23:08,260
Sorry about that.

362
00:23:09,763 --> 00:23:11,764
I don't know...

363
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:22,274
Tell me more about Zachariah.

364
00:23:22,442 --> 00:23:25,820
Orrin, you may ask for a lawyer
at any time.

365
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:28,489
- Then my parents will know, right?
- Yes.

366
00:23:29,449 --> 00:23:30,491
That's okay.

367
00:23:31,159 --> 00:23:33,828
Zachariah and the Z Krew.

368
00:23:33,995 --> 00:23:37,039
Why should I tell you?
You know what I'm thinking.

369
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:42,670
Yeah. But it would be more polite
if you said it aloud, for their benefit.

370
00:23:43,338 --> 00:23:46,882
You can't really read minds, can you?

371
00:23:47,050 --> 00:23:49,176
Shrewd insight. No, of course I can't.

372
00:23:49,344 --> 00:23:51,804
Then how'd you do that then?
Call me out like that?

373
00:23:51,972 --> 00:23:54,557
You scratched your poison oak.
My colleagues tell me...

374
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:57,017
...that only grows in one place
around here.

375
00:23:57,185 --> 00:24:00,146
- Up at Mr. Winston's.
- Fudge.

376
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:02,648
Yeah. So tell me more
about Zachariah.

377
00:24:03,859 --> 00:24:06,819
- I can't.
- Really?

378
00:24:07,362 --> 00:24:11,365
Orrin, we can let this go,
or we can take it to the next level.

379
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:14,201
And that's gonna involve your parents
and lawyers.

380
00:24:18,874 --> 00:24:22,877
Zachariah was a lumberjack,
hundreds of years ago.

381
00:24:23,044 --> 00:24:26,213
A log fell on him in the river
and pinned him by the arm.

382
00:24:26,381 --> 00:24:29,884
His logging crew tried,
but they couldn't get him out.

383
00:24:30,051 --> 00:24:32,386
The river was rising,
and a snowstorm was coming.

384
00:24:32,554 --> 00:24:34,555
They figured that
he was done for anyway...

385
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:38,058
...so they left him there,
left him for dead.

386
00:24:38,226 --> 00:24:40,603
Zachariah was so angry at them
for leaving him...

387
00:24:40,812 --> 00:24:44,607
...he chopped off his arm to free himself,
then went back to the lumber camp...

388
00:24:44,816 --> 00:24:47,568
...and hacked every one
of his workmates to death.

389
00:24:47,736 --> 00:24:50,404
Then chopped them up
and put their heads in trees.

390
00:24:50,572 --> 00:24:51,947
Cool.

391
00:24:52,115 --> 00:24:54,408
- The lumber camp where they died?
- Uh-huh.

392
00:24:54,951 --> 00:24:57,870
This is it, right here.

393
00:24:58,038 --> 00:25:01,832
- This school is the exact same spot.
- Wow.

394
00:25:02,250 --> 00:25:05,085
- And Z Krew?
- It's like a secret club.

395
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:09,590
We go up in the woods and do stuff.
Zachariah is like our leader.

396
00:25:11,259 --> 00:25:13,886
- Who's, like, the deputy leader?
- I don't know.

397
00:25:14,262 --> 00:25:16,096
- No?
- Come on.

398
00:25:16,264 --> 00:25:17,264
We wear masks.

399
00:25:17,432 --> 00:25:20,434
The only person you know
is the person that asked you to join.

400
00:25:20,602 --> 00:25:21,727
Who was that?

401
00:25:25,065 --> 00:25:26,232
Bryan.

402
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:28,901
Hey, man, wait up.

403
00:25:29,444 --> 00:25:30,611
There he is.

404
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:32,655
- I got this.
- Please, I got this.

405
00:25:35,867 --> 00:25:37,743
After you.

406
00:25:48,463 --> 00:25:49,505
Nice.

407
00:25:49,673 --> 00:25:53,842
- Who initiated you to Z Krew, Bryan?
- Guy that jumped me in left last year.

408
00:25:54,010 --> 00:25:55,678
- Who runs Z Krew?
- I don't know.

409
00:25:55,887 --> 00:25:58,764
Hard to believe
you didn't recognize anybody's voice.

410
00:25:58,932 --> 00:26:00,432
No talking on Z Krew ops.

411
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,810
We only communicate by note
and sign language.

412
00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:04,395
That's the whole fun of it.

413
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:09,483
Look, Z Krew's about running around
in the woods, playing warriors.

414
00:26:09,651 --> 00:26:11,277
Nobody gets killed.

415
00:26:11,444 --> 00:26:14,029
Z Krew's got nothing to do
with Justin's murder.

416
00:26:14,197 --> 00:26:16,156
- Do you?
- No.

417
00:26:19,828 --> 00:26:20,995
You want my guess?

418
00:26:21,162 --> 00:26:24,790
Guesswork is inappropriate
for this sort of situation, Bryan.

419
00:26:24,958 --> 00:26:26,166
Guesswork's okay.

420
00:26:28,461 --> 00:26:30,421
Cassie.

421
00:26:31,464 --> 00:26:33,799
- She's in it somehow.
- How so?

422
00:26:33,967 --> 00:26:36,135
Justin was...

423
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:38,012
He was big in love with her.

424
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:41,682
She wouldn't deal,
and he didn't like it.

425
00:26:41,850 --> 00:26:45,811
I saw them arguing, both real mad,
a couple days ago.

426
00:26:45,979 --> 00:26:49,023
And now she's totally freaked out
about his death.

427
00:26:50,358 --> 00:26:53,902
- So you know...
- Many of us are upset, Bryan.

428
00:26:54,070 --> 00:26:57,156
- Does Cassie have a boyfriend?
- No.

429
00:26:57,324 --> 00:27:00,659
So, what do you think happened?
Cassie killed him?

430
00:27:00,827 --> 00:27:03,370
- That's ridiculous.
- Let him answer.

431
00:27:04,164 --> 00:27:06,832
Hey, ask her.

432
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:09,710
All I'm saying, it wasn't me.

433
00:27:11,212 --> 00:27:13,088
Do you know
where we could find Cassie?

434
00:27:13,256 --> 00:27:15,716
I'm sure that she has nothing
to do with this.

435
00:27:17,677 --> 00:27:21,889
But I will have someone
fetch her for you.

436
00:27:26,394 --> 00:27:28,687
- Gave you a little trouble, huh?
- No.

437
00:27:29,856 --> 00:27:32,608
- Hey, guys.
- What the hell is that?

438
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:34,568
- What happened to you?
- Old age.

439
00:27:35,070 --> 00:27:36,737
Shut up, you.

440
00:27:36,905 --> 00:27:39,531
- What are you doing here?
- Gee, thanks for the welcome.

441
00:27:39,699 --> 00:27:42,951
- No, I mean... You know what I mean.
- Lisbon wanted an extra hand.

442
00:27:43,119 --> 00:27:45,788
If we're gonna have to interview
all students and staff.

443
00:27:45,997 --> 00:27:48,582
Seriously, this is the biggest they had?

444
00:27:48,750 --> 00:27:50,084
- Hey, Van Pelt.
- Hey, boss.

445
00:27:50,752 --> 00:27:53,087
We're short a girl
by the name Cassie Miniver.

446
00:27:53,254 --> 00:27:55,130
Bryan says Justin
was in love with Cassie.

447
00:27:55,298 --> 00:27:57,424
Recently saw them in a fierce argument.

448
00:27:57,592 --> 00:28:00,260
Oh, Cassie. Yeah,
she brought Maclean a cup of tea.

449
00:28:00,428 --> 00:28:03,097
Yeah, we wanted to question her,
but she's gone.

450
00:28:03,264 --> 00:28:05,641
- Interesting.
- Anybody else missing?

451
00:28:05,809 --> 00:28:07,434
No, there isn't.

452
00:28:07,602 --> 00:28:09,770
So she's most likely running,
not abducted.

453
00:28:09,938 --> 00:28:11,772
- Precisely.
- What do you think, boss?

454
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:13,816
Chief Brody's setting up a search.

455
00:28:14,025 --> 00:28:16,610
We should start looking
in the woods around the school.

456
00:28:16,778 --> 00:28:20,572
Oh, that sounds horribly tedious.
Shout if you need me.

457
00:28:21,241 --> 00:28:23,742
Go ahead, relax. Enjoy yourself.

458
00:28:23,910 --> 00:28:27,413
God forbid
you should do anything tedious.

459
00:28:30,917 --> 00:28:33,293
- Cassie!
- Cassie!

460
00:28:33,461 --> 00:28:35,295
- Cassie!
- Cassie!

461
00:28:35,463 --> 00:28:37,673
- Cassie!
- Cassie!

462
00:28:37,841 --> 00:28:39,800
Cassie!

463
00:28:39,968 --> 00:28:41,927
Cassie!

464
00:28:42,095 --> 00:28:43,595
- Cassie!
- Cassie!

465
00:28:43,763 --> 00:28:46,140
- Can I ask you something?
- Yeah.

466
00:28:46,307 --> 00:28:51,603
Would you...? Have you ever read
your co-worker's personnel files?

467
00:28:52,355 --> 00:28:54,481
No. Why?

468
00:28:54,649 --> 00:28:58,777
No. I'm good. Neither did I. Okay.

469
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:24,303
Hey.

470
00:29:26,514 --> 00:29:28,974
- Hi.
- Where you headed?

471
00:29:30,685 --> 00:29:32,519
- Into town.
- Excellent.

472
00:29:32,687 --> 00:29:34,354
That's exactly where I need to go.

473
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:37,983
All right.

474
00:29:44,032 --> 00:29:46,700
Thanks. Grateful.

475
00:29:59,005 --> 00:30:02,508
- Would you shut the gate for me, please?
- Nope.

476
00:30:03,218 --> 00:30:05,677
- Why?
- Well, as soon as I get out of the car...

477
00:30:05,845 --> 00:30:07,387
...you'll drive away without me.

478
00:30:09,766 --> 00:30:12,017
Why on Earth would I do that?

479
00:30:12,185 --> 00:30:15,395
The three Furies. Fear, shame, guilt.

480
00:30:15,563 --> 00:30:18,857
- What?
- The heart wants what the heart wants.

481
00:30:19,025 --> 00:30:22,528
It won't be denied.
It makes us do bad things.

482
00:30:23,404 --> 00:30:25,739
What are you talking about?

483
00:30:26,074 --> 00:30:28,575
Cassie, I have a gift for you.

484
00:30:33,248 --> 00:30:35,791
Cassie? Needn't be shy.

485
00:30:41,214 --> 00:30:44,091
- Hi.
- Hi.

486
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:49,179
Here.

487
00:30:52,725 --> 00:30:54,476
Try it on.

488
00:31:01,401 --> 00:31:03,277
Beautiful.

489
00:31:20,795 --> 00:31:22,880
Ta-da.

490
00:31:23,047 --> 00:31:24,298
What is this?

491
00:31:24,841 --> 00:31:27,175
Mr. Maclean
was helping Cassie run away.

492
00:31:28,970 --> 00:31:31,555
- Why?
- He didn't want us to speak to her.

493
00:31:31,723 --> 00:31:34,266
- Because...?
- I have nothing to say.

494
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:37,019
Nonsense. You have plenty to say.

495
00:31:37,186 --> 00:31:40,063
He wanted her to go
before we got a chance to talk to her...

496
00:31:40,231 --> 00:31:42,482
...and find out
that she and he were having...

497
00:31:42,650 --> 00:31:46,570
...what you would call,
"sexual relations."

498
00:31:48,031 --> 00:31:50,616
- Is that true?
- I'm saying nothing. I admit nothing.

499
00:31:50,825 --> 00:31:54,494
I wanna talk to my lawyer.
Cassie, don't say anything.

500
00:31:55,705 --> 00:31:58,290
- You miserable little pervert.
- That's enough, chief.

501
00:31:58,458 --> 00:32:00,375
- She assaulted me.
- I don't think so.

502
00:32:00,543 --> 00:32:02,294
We're going back to Sacramento.

503
00:32:02,462 --> 00:32:04,838
Now, you can either come
of your own accord...

504
00:32:05,006 --> 00:32:07,090
...or we can arrest you. Which is it?

505
00:32:09,844 --> 00:32:11,595
Fine.

506
00:32:13,222 --> 00:32:15,015
Good choice.

507
00:32:20,855 --> 00:32:22,648
We didn't...

508
00:32:23,191 --> 00:32:25,233
We weren't, no.

509
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:30,405
Cassie, look at me.
It's very easy to see when you're lying.

510
00:32:30,573 --> 00:32:34,618
You get a little pulse going
in your neck just there. Yeah.

511
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:37,913
Always best
to tell Agent Lisbon the truth.

512
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:42,918
Did Mr. Maclean
have sexual relations with you?

513
00:32:47,465 --> 00:32:49,091
It's okay.

514
00:32:50,134 --> 00:32:51,802
Yes, he did.

515
00:32:52,303 --> 00:32:55,722
- One time? Or more than that?
- More.

516
00:32:56,391 --> 00:32:58,934
Maybe twice a week
for a few months.

517
00:32:59,102 --> 00:33:01,645
You know that
by having sexual relations with you...

518
00:33:01,813 --> 00:33:04,606
...Mr. Maclean
was committing a crime, right?

519
00:33:04,774 --> 00:33:07,651
- I guess.
- Was it consensual?

520
00:33:08,528 --> 00:33:09,695
I guess.

521
00:33:10,613 --> 00:33:11,822
You guess?

522
00:33:12,615 --> 00:33:15,283
Did you want Mr. Maclean
to have sex with you?

523
00:33:15,451 --> 00:33:18,620
- No, ma'am.
- So he coerced you?

524
00:33:19,914 --> 00:33:21,039
No, ma'am.

525
00:33:21,916 --> 00:33:24,960
- I don't understand.
- I was scared.

526
00:33:25,128 --> 00:33:27,337
Scared of who? Mr. Maclean?

527
00:33:27,922 --> 00:33:31,842
- No, he's just a sad creep.
- Who then?

528
00:33:36,639 --> 00:33:39,057
You can talk freely, Cassie.
You're safe here.

529
00:33:39,225 --> 00:33:42,102
- Nowhere is safe.
- Zachariah made you do it?

530
00:33:45,356 --> 00:33:48,108
A zombie lumberjack
made you sleep with Mr. Maclean?

531
00:33:48,609 --> 00:33:50,027
He told me I had to.

532
00:33:50,194 --> 00:33:53,947
Cassie, you know
that Zachariah doesn't exist?

533
00:33:54,115 --> 00:33:56,908
You know that kid that they found
chopped up in the woods?

534
00:33:57,076 --> 00:33:58,618
He thought the same thing.

535
00:33:59,078 --> 00:34:01,997
Okay, how does Zachariah
tell you his wishes?

536
00:34:05,376 --> 00:34:08,754
- Through somebody from Z Krew maybe?
- I've said too much already.

537
00:34:08,963 --> 00:34:12,799
I don't wanna say anymore.
Please, don't make me.

538
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:16,887
I'll be right back.

539
00:34:26,981 --> 00:34:31,234
Cassie made a statement.
Charge Mr. Maclean with statutory rape.

540
00:34:31,402 --> 00:34:33,320
Will do, boss.

541
00:34:38,576 --> 00:34:39,785
Sex with a minor.

542
00:34:40,495 --> 00:34:43,080
Tell you what,
things look very bad for you right now.

543
00:34:43,247 --> 00:34:47,084
I was kind and caring
to a troubled girl. That's all.

544
00:34:47,543 --> 00:34:50,712
Yeah, that's what they all say
until the lab tests come back.

545
00:34:51,506 --> 00:34:54,382
The way we figure this,
Justin was in love with Cassie...

546
00:34:54,550 --> 00:34:56,885
- ...and found out you were abusing her...
- Please.

547
00:34:57,053 --> 00:35:00,388
And threatened to tell the authorities.
So you clubbed him to death...

548
00:35:00,556 --> 00:35:02,516
- ...you thought, and buried him.
- No. No.

549
00:35:02,683 --> 00:35:06,853
No? Well, that's what we're thinking.

550
00:35:08,606 --> 00:35:10,357
How are we wrong?

551
00:35:10,858 --> 00:35:13,819
Did he attack you?
Was it self-defense, maybe?

552
00:35:14,028 --> 00:35:18,031
I want my lawyer.
I'm saying nothing more to you people.

553
00:35:19,700 --> 00:35:23,787
- We got nothing to put him with Justin.
- We need a confession.

554
00:35:23,955 --> 00:35:26,498
- You won't get one.
- Why won't we get one?

555
00:35:26,666 --> 00:35:29,042
A prize for the first one
to tell me the answer.

556
00:35:29,210 --> 00:35:31,294
Just tell us your damn theory.

557
00:35:31,462 --> 00:35:33,922
I will do that on our way back
to Bright Arch.

558
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:36,758
We need to get there in time
for the sacred fire ritual.

559
00:35:36,926 --> 00:35:39,469
Rigsby, let's have a quick cup of tea,
then we'll go.

560
00:35:39,637 --> 00:35:42,264
Explain first, then we'll go.

561
00:35:42,723 --> 00:35:44,891
Sacred fire?

562
00:35:46,102 --> 00:35:48,061
Hello, kids.

563
00:35:48,479 --> 00:35:50,856
Good to see you all again.

564
00:35:52,066 --> 00:35:54,359
- Pretty dramatic few days, huh?
- Oh, yeah.

565
00:35:55,570 --> 00:35:58,947
Probably heard a lot of crazy stuff
about what's been going on.

566
00:35:59,365 --> 00:36:03,827
Well, don't worry about it.
Life goes on.

567
00:36:05,580 --> 00:36:08,915
Your teachers thought it'd be good
to carry on with the fire ceremony.

568
00:36:09,083 --> 00:36:12,043
- Everyone okay with that?
- Yeah.

569
00:36:12,211 --> 00:36:14,087
Excellent.

570
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:16,423
I thought we'd start
with a ghost story.

571
00:36:17,592 --> 00:36:20,385
- You all know about Zachariah, yeah?
- We do.

572
00:36:21,596 --> 00:36:24,514
- But we don't talk about him.
- It's bad luck.

573
00:36:25,975 --> 00:36:27,475
Zachariah doesn't scare me.

574
00:36:29,812 --> 00:36:32,147
So everyone knows
about that terrible evening...

575
00:36:32,315 --> 00:36:36,234
...when Zachariah hacked
his former friends to pieces, yeah?

576
00:36:36,694 --> 00:36:38,361
What a lot of people don't know...

577
00:36:38,779 --> 00:36:42,324
...is what happened
after that horrible incident.

578
00:36:47,121 --> 00:36:52,042
As punishment,
the townspeople gathered together...

579
00:36:52,210 --> 00:36:54,711
...and built a huge bonfire...

580
00:36:54,879 --> 00:36:56,546
...right here...

581
00:36:57,131 --> 00:36:58,673
...on this very spot.

582
00:36:58,841 --> 00:37:02,636
And they burned Zachariah alive.

583
00:37:03,137 --> 00:37:07,307
And as the flames melted the flesh
from his body...

584
00:37:07,850 --> 00:37:09,517
...Zachariah didn't scream.

585
00:37:09,685 --> 00:37:15,899
He just smiled at those watching,
and he made a solemn vow.

586
00:37:16,651 --> 00:37:20,195
That whenever someone does evil
in these woods...

587
00:37:20,363 --> 00:37:25,116
...if you call Zachariah's name three
times and mark the ground with a Z...

588
00:37:25,284 --> 00:37:28,286
...then he will rise from the grave
and he will take them.

589
00:37:28,454 --> 00:37:30,413
Yeah, right.

590
00:37:34,961 --> 00:37:38,004
If the sinner doesn't confess his sins,
if he doesn't repent...

591
00:37:38,172 --> 00:37:42,801
...then Zachariah will drag them down
into his ghastly lair...

592
00:37:42,969 --> 00:37:47,472
...to suffer with him in black darkness
for all eternity.

593
00:37:49,267 --> 00:37:51,559
- That's it?
- Yes, that's it.

594
00:37:51,727 --> 00:37:53,186
That was weak, dude.

595
00:37:57,400 --> 00:38:00,485
Well, it's only weak
if the curse isn't true.

596
00:38:01,028 --> 00:38:05,365
We all know that evil has been done
in these woods.

597
00:38:06,534 --> 00:38:10,287
But is there anyone here willing
to call Zachariah's name?

598
00:38:13,374 --> 00:38:14,708
Anyone?

599
00:38:18,379 --> 00:38:20,005
Zachariah?

600
00:38:22,258 --> 00:38:23,466
Zachariah.

601
00:38:25,428 --> 00:38:26,970
Zachariah.

602
00:38:33,227 --> 00:38:35,228
Told you. Weak.

603
00:38:36,814 --> 00:38:38,982
You forgot the most important part.

604
00:38:42,528 --> 00:38:44,779
You have to mark the ground with a Z.

605
00:39:06,427 --> 00:39:08,011
Guess he's on vacation.

606
00:39:14,769 --> 00:39:18,772
Elliot, was it you? Did you kill Justin?

607
00:39:21,150 --> 00:39:23,526
This is your last chance.
Did you kill Justin?

608
00:39:23,944 --> 00:39:26,279
Yes. Yes, it was me.

609
00:39:29,575 --> 00:39:31,201
Saved. That was close.

610
00:39:37,291 --> 00:39:39,584
- Oh, hey, Rigsby.
- Hey.

611
00:39:43,798 --> 00:39:46,841
I knew it was a joke.
I was just kidding.

612
00:39:47,009 --> 00:39:51,805
No, you're a liar and a murderer, Elliot.
Everyone can see that.

613
00:39:53,307 --> 00:39:57,310
- Whoa, whoa, whoa. A little help here.
- Give it up kid. Come on, it's over.

614
00:40:01,315 --> 00:40:04,818
Justin was an insect.
He shouldn't have interfered.

615
00:40:04,985 --> 00:40:07,904
Yes, you had
a sweet little system going.

616
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:10,740
He kept the kids in line
with messages from Zachariah.

617
00:40:10,908 --> 00:40:13,952
And kept Maclean in line
with blackmail.

618
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:18,790
Protect Elliot and let the Z Krew rule,
or be exposed as a habitual rapist.

619
00:40:18,958 --> 00:40:21,751
- You're a very clever young man.
- Yes, I am.

620
00:40:23,170 --> 00:40:26,423
That's why my parents abandoned me
in this dump.

621
00:40:27,216 --> 00:40:30,844
I'm too clever for them. And for you.

622
00:40:31,679 --> 00:40:33,304
You haven't really caught me.

623
00:40:33,472 --> 00:40:35,849
I'm a minor.
Nothing bad will happen to me.

624
00:40:36,016 --> 00:40:39,769
Then why don't you tell us
why you killed Justin? For the record.

625
00:40:39,937 --> 00:40:41,229
You know why.

626
00:40:42,690 --> 00:40:45,984
Justin was always soft on Cassie.

627
00:40:46,152 --> 00:40:47,652
But when he found out...

628
00:40:47,862 --> 00:40:50,780
...what she was doing with Maclean
on my order...

629
00:40:51,365 --> 00:40:54,284
...he got angry,
threatened to ruin everything.

630
00:40:54,452 --> 00:40:58,288
And I tried to shut him up
with a message from Zachariah...

631
00:40:58,456 --> 00:41:01,791
...but he wouldn't back off.
He laughed at me.

632
00:41:04,879 --> 00:41:07,005
He shouldn't have done that.

633
00:41:11,051 --> 00:41:13,720
I don't like being laughed at.

634
00:41:16,807 --> 00:41:20,143
Well, goodbye, Elliot.

635
00:41:21,061 --> 00:41:22,520
Hey.

636
00:41:24,940 --> 00:41:26,524
How did you know it was me?

637
00:41:30,696 --> 00:41:33,490
When Cassie brought Maclean tea
in a cup with Z's on it...

638
00:41:33,657 --> 00:41:35,325
...that was a warning from you.

639
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:37,452
You were first
to bring forth Zachariah.

640
00:41:37,620 --> 00:41:41,289
You've been at this school longer
than anyone, with no desire to leave.

641
00:41:41,457 --> 00:41:44,167
The sacred fire ceremony
confirmed my hunch.

642
00:41:44,585 --> 00:41:47,587
Everybody else was scared
that I was invoking Zachariah.

643
00:41:47,755 --> 00:41:53,426
But you were contemptuous and cynical.
A true artist watching a cheap imitator.

644
00:41:53,594 --> 00:41:57,472
Until fear made you a believer.

645
00:41:58,140 --> 00:42:01,100
It can do that to you. Bye.

646
00:42:03,771 --> 00:42:05,647
Sit down.

647
00:42:08,275 --> 00:42:10,151
I appreciate it.

648
00:42:12,530 --> 00:42:14,197
- Thank you.
- Well...

649
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:18,284
There he is.

650
00:42:19,203 --> 00:42:21,162
Here I am.

651
00:42:23,666 --> 00:42:28,753
I was just telling Mr. and Mrs. Prentiss
it was you that found their son's killer.

652
00:42:28,963 --> 00:42:31,506
Yes, I'm very sorry for your loss.

653
00:42:31,674 --> 00:42:34,968
Thank you. Thank you so much.

654
00:42:36,637 --> 00:42:40,682
We're very grateful.
It gives us some kind of closure at least.

655
00:42:47,314 --> 00:42:49,857
Your son died bravely.

656
00:42:50,150 --> 00:42:52,986
He saved a young girl in trouble.
You should be very proud.

657
00:43:02,663 --> 00:43:05,081
- Thank you, again.
- Absolutely.

658
00:43:05,249 --> 00:43:08,084
- Take care.
- Thank you.

